docs {
  # Verifying the AgentRun incident trigger

  Requests 4-8 demonstrate confirmed contract drift on a fresh
  `contract-drift-demo-<timestamp>` source:

  - `4` creates the source (a new one per run, so the demo is deterministic
    without resetting volumes) and stores its id as `drift_source_id`.
  - `5` ingests the v1 schema — the first snapshot auto-becomes the baseline.
  - `6`, `7`, `8` ingest the v2 schema (the `title` field removed). Drift is
    only confirmed after `CONTRACT_BASELINE_CONFIRMATION_POLLS = 3` identical
    observations, so `6` and `7` return `drift_event: null` and the breaking
    event fires on `8` (`event_type == "breaking"`, `removed_fields: ["title"]`).

  Per `docs/.plans/ai-augmented-observatory-agent-mcp.md` Phase 1, that
  auto-creates an `Observation` (`tags: ["incident", severity]`) + a
  `pending` `AgentRun`, in the same transaction as the drift event.

  There is no read endpoint for `AgentRun`/incident `Observation`s yet —
  that lands in Phase 4/5 of the plan, at which point this note gets
  replaced by a real Bruno request. Until then, verify directly:

  ```bash
  # tags is a plain `json` column (not `jsonb`) — cast explicitly for containment checks.
  docker compose exec -T ingestor-db psql -U postgres -d api_obs_ingestor -c \
    "SELECT id, source, tags, raw_data->>'drift_event_id' AS drift_event_id
     FROM observations WHERE tags::jsonb @> '[\"incident\"]' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 5;"

  docker compose exec -T ingestor-db psql -U postgres -d api_obs_ingestor -c \
    "SELECT id, observation_id, status FROM agent_runs ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 5;"
  ```

  Expect one new row in each table per breaking/critical drift event, with
  `agent_runs.status = 'pending'` (no analysis runs until Phase 3's
  LangGraph agent exists).

  This GET /health request is included as a smoke check so `bru run` does
  not skip this collection folder.
}
